From ac2c3c4dfb3d254895781a3e84c38146762ed4e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TC Lowe <111537227+TCLowe1982@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 3 Aug 2026 13:38:28 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] feat(generation): wire prompt-context contributions into
 the generation route
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Collects contributions from active agents that registered a contributor and
places them through the existing agent-injection machinery: preset section
replacement when the active preset declares a slot, otherwise a separate
injection message, skipping placement entirely when the preset owns it.
Contributions also join contextInjections so downstream agents that opt into
pre-generation injections see them like any other.

Only agents with a registered contributor are made eligible for a preset
placement slot, so no slot is reserved for an agent that supplies nothing.
long-term-memory is excluded from the generic pass because it already has a
dedicated call above; this adds no second path for it.

Acceptance is reported after dispatch, at the same two points the long-term
memory path uses, and only for contributions that actually reached the
prompt — one dropped by preset placement is never reported as shipped.

Gated on !regenerateMessageId to match long-term memory: a re-roll reuses the
context cached on the original generation rather than recomputing, so the
generic pass is skipped and nothing is reported for it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
